BUNDLED COMPONENTS
------------------

Trixnity -- Kotlin Multiplatform SDK for Matrix
  Copyright connect2x GmbH. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Upstream: https://github.com/connect2x-de/trixnity
  Used as a published Maven dependency. An unmodified copy of part of the client
  module is vendored at `trixnity-src/` as developer reference material only; it is
  not compiled and is not on the runtime classpath.
  Full text and notes: `trixnity-src/LICENSE`, `trixnity-src/NOTICE`.

webrtc-java -- WebRTC for desktop platforms running Java
  Copyright 2019 Alex Andres. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Upstream: https://github.com/devopvoid/webrtc-java
  `webrtc-java-lib/` is Orbit's in-tree build of the Java API layer and IS compiled
  (`include(":webrtc-java-lib")` in settings.gradle.kts). `webrtc_sources/` is the
  matching set of Java interface sources, kept for reference.
  Full text and notes: `webrtc-java-lib/LICENSE`, `webrtc-java-lib/NOTICE`.

webrtc-java fork -- Orbit's modifications
  `webrtc-java-fork/` carries the Apache-2.0 LICENSE and NOTICE inherited from
  upstream. It also contains the JNI layer (`webrtc-jni/`) and a bundled build of
  WebRTC itself.
  Full text and notes: `webrtc-java-fork/LICENSE`, `webrtc-java-fork/NOTICE`.

WebRTC
  Bundled inside `webrtc-java-fork/` and shipped in the native library
  (`webrtc-java-orbit-windows-x86_64.dll`). Available under a 3-clause BSD license.
  Details: https://webrtc.github.io/webrtc-org/license

LiveKit
  Bundled as `livekit.dll` / `livekit_ffi.dll`. Licensed under the Apache License,
  Version 2.0. Upstream: https://github.com/livekit/client-sdk-flutter
  Orbit's own native LiveKit media session (`orbit_livekit_audio.dll`,
  `orbit_livekit_video.dll`) is original work, licensed under the same terms as the
  rest of Orbit.

NOTE ON MODIFICATIONS
---------------------

Apache-2.0 section 4(b) requires modified files to carry prominent notices stating
the change. Orbit's modifications to `webrtc-java-fork/` are scoped to that
directory and its README documents them; the vendored reference trees listed above
(`trixnity-src/`, `webrtc-java-lib/`, `webrtc_sources/`) are unmodified upstream
source and say so in their own NOTICE files.

THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES
------------------------

Orbit depends on, but does not redistribute source for, Kotlin, Compose Multiplatform,
Trixnity and its transitive Ktor/kotlinx.serialization/Koin dependencies, JNA, Okio
and the Room, SQLCipher and Trixnity crypto stack. Each remains under its own license
as published; see the dependency declarations in `app/build.gradle.kts` and
`settings.gradle.kts`. The packaged Windows installer additionally bundles a Java
runtime under the Eclipse Temurin/Adoptium terms, whose license files ship in
`runtime/legal/` inside the installed application.
